Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:11:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] port 77794e34 + b72f56e0: quoted tool-call markup inside
 a string argument stays exact (#4078)

77794e34: a </parameter> inside a call the value itself quotes (more quoted openers than </function> before it),
or one followed by the same parameter name again, is part of the value; prose between two calls still ends the
first call. The streaming scanner walks from the value's start so a quoted opener counts. b72f56e0 (mandatory):
only a whole quoted `<function=NAME>` followed by a parameter or close keeps a value open; a bare `<function=`
in prose or code no longer swallows every later </parameter> (call as content / never finished when streaming).
77794e34 is a clean cherry-pick, b72f56e0 applies with -C1 (one context hunk). serve/frontend.py only;
test_quoted_call_values.py comes along.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
